  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Which of the following vector-valued functions are continuous at $t=1?$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\u27e8\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,\\,2{t}^{2},\\,|t-1|\u27e9 \\\\ g(t) & =\u27e88{t}^{2}-2,\\,{2}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\u27e9 \\\\ h(t) & =\u27e85t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t+3),\\,7\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "A vector-valued function is continuous at a point if and only if each of its components is continuous at that point.\n\nLet's consider the functions one-by-one. \n\n- The function $f(t)$ is continuous at $t=1$ because each of its components $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t$, $2{t}^{2}$ and $|t-1|$ are continuous at $t=1.$\n\n- The function $g(t)$ is continuous at $t=1$ because each of its components $8{t}^{2}-2$, ${2}^{t}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$ are continuous at $t=1.$\n\n- The function $h(t)$ is continuous at $t=1$ because each of its components $5t$, $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t+3)$ and the constant function $7$ are continuous at $t=1.$\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n$\\,$ All the functions are continuous at $t=1$",
